      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C25", "C29", "C35"]
    },
    {
      "family": "associated_nonvoting_records",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C22"]
    },
    {
      "family": "associated_nonvoting_records",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C26", "C34"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental absolute oral bioavailability value for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific fasted-state solubility, dissolution, or permeability data.",
    "No IV comparator or human PK data for the query.",
    "The apatinib L2 low value lacks species, dose, formulation, and comparator detail and conflicts with its L1 'good' label, leaving its transferability uncertain.",
    "Most context records do not explicitly match the fasted condition; only tolvaptan food-independence is directly relevant.",
    "C20 is a predicted HIA-based value with ambiguous F30% notation and was not used as a primary vote."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high: F >= 20% is better supported by multiple transferable high absolute-bioavailability contexts, especially the benzamide/indazole and lipophilic benzamide scaffolds (venadaparib, tolvaptan, imidafenacin, ACT-1004-1239, lenvatinib), reinforced by new L2 preclinical values above 20% and tolvaptan food independence. The apatinib 10-20% L2 record is internally inconsistent and less structurally aligned, and ilomastat is a non-transferable peptidomimetic; solubility/lipophilicity risks are noted but do not affirmatively establish F < 20%."
}

